WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.036
-Our next guest is a talented
actress you know from her work

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.804
as Kamala Khan on the hit series
"Ms. Marvel."

00:00:05.804 --> 00:00:08.875
All six episodes are available
now on Disney+.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.142
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:12.578
-Oh. But no, I've spoken
too much already.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.448
No, no, no, I'm not going to
talk about this at all.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.482
-Kamala?

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.618
-Your mother will get
very upset.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.753
-So this belonged to Aisha
and you really have no idea

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:24.323
what happened to her?
-Oh, beta, speak up a bit.

00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:26.392
My old ears are not --

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.627
-Kamala.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:34.634
-Please welcome to the show
Iman Vellani, everyone!

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.636
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:41.841 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:47.046 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.815
Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:52.919
I am particularly very excited
about this one

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:56.922
because our producer Sana who
was on your Show in like 2016...

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:59.859
-Yes, here's Sana. She's one of
the producers of "Ms. Marvel."

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.294
And she was here.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.763
And I guess you have watched
this interview.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.232
-Oh, yes. It was the first thing
I watched after I read

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.766
the "Ms. Marvel" comics
for the first time.

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.302
And I was, like,
obsessed with her.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.071
I was like, "How did she get
a job at Marvel Comics

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.907
and be brown and a woman
at the same time?"

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.442
-Seems like you'd be happier
about it.

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.944
You seem really mad about it.
-I was so jealous.

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:20.813
[ Laughter ]
Me being like 15 years old.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:22.748
But yeah, I was obsessed
with her.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.917
And now six years later I'm here
talking about "Ms. Marvel."

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.986
And she's here too somewhere.
-She is. She's backstage.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.955
It was nice to see her again.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:32.291
But again, I think this is
the part that's so sweet.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.560
So, you obviously you cared
about this comic book

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.597
and now you're playing Marvel's
first Muslim superhero.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.099
And she's a teenager
and you're a teenager.

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:43.402
And I can't even imagine --
also you're a comic book fan --

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:46.506
of what this whole process was
like, ending up with this part.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.874
-My life is overwhelmingly good
right now.

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.810
[ Laughter ]
-That's good. Live it up.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.411
There's no reason to be shy
about it.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:55.347
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:58.952
Is it true, were you the kind of
person who you did

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.486
spend your allowance on
comic books?

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.388
-All $20.
-20 bucks?

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.422
-Yeah.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:05.024
-Is that a good allowance
these days?

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.392
Because I have to start
figuring out --

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.027
-No, I had to make
an Excel spreadsheet

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.262
and, like, talk to my parents.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.863
I'm like look, these are
my expenses

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.565
as a 15-year-old
high school kid.

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.600
I need comics.
I need McDonald's.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.903
I need clothes, I guess? Yeah.

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.938
But it was just
McDonald's and comics.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.639
-And you were a Marvel kid?
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:22.508
-Is that accurate?
-But it was mostly Iron Man.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.711
So I obviously fell in love with
the MCU first and then

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.513
my high school was right across
from a comic book store,

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.882
and I was like,
"I need more Iron Man."

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.218
So I read every "Invincible
Iron Man" comic I could get.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.920
And then I ran into Ironheart

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.288
'cause I thought she was
Iron Man.

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:37.489
That was wrong.
And Kamala was on the cover

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:38.558
of one of those comics

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.460
and that's when I fell in love
with her.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.930
-I mean, I think, it is
important, you know, obviously

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.666
so special to have this kind of
representation in comics.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.367
What was it like the first time
you saw "Ms. Marvel"?

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:51.471
-Ah. In person? In the mirror?

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.306
[ Laughter ]
No, it was crazy.

00:02:54.306 --> 00:02:56.442
She felt so different than all
the other Muslim teenagers

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:58.511
I was used to seeing
in mainstream media.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:02.448
She was using her culture as
something that guided her.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.450
And it wasn't something
she neglected at all.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.786
And on top of that
she was a huge fan.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.121
And the show is -- The comics

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.824
were never about being Muslim
or being Pakistani.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.294
It was about this
superhero-obsessed dork who just

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.895
happens to be
Muslim and Pakistani.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:17.363
And that's how I felt
in real life.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.865
And it was really comforting
reading those comics.

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:21.700
-Well, it certainly --
I think they ended up

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.603
on the right person
for the part.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.606
So there's a really cool
animation style in this show

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.407
as well, outside of
the live action,

00:03:28.407 --> 00:03:32.344
and it's so visually pleasant
and pleasing to watch.

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:35.615
Were you also someone who was
drawn to art growing up?

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.816
I feel weird say growing up

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.584
because I feel like
that hasn't finished yet.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.352
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:41.654
-I'm an adult?

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.456
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.258
No, but I was.
I was really into art.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.293
It's funny.
During one of our quarantines,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.762
I made a little stop-motion with
my Iron Man

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.163
and Kamala action figures.

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:55.034
And I sent it to Kevin Feige and
our producers with zero context.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:58.037
It was like literally my action
figures dancing or something.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.807
And then they really liked that.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:05.043
And we ended up changing our
episode one opening animation

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:07.046
to be a stop motion instead of
like a regular animation.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.215
-So Kevin Feige, who,
if anybody follows

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.883
the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.585
this is the man
who's pulling the strings.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.354
He's sort of the brain
behind it all.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.122
Did you feel nervous
when you first met him

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:19.358
or were you right away sending
him weird stop-motion animation?

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.426
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.461
-So I didn't -- I stared at him

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:25.097
until he left the first time
I met him.

00:04:25.097 --> 00:04:27.233
I like couldn't be a human
at all. I lost all function.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.001
-And do you think he left
because you were staring at him?

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.002
-Possibly.
-Possibly, yeah.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:31.570
-He's really awkward.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.207
And if you're awkward, then it's
just a double whammy.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.042
It's terrible,
but Sana was like,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:37.510
"Okay, so he's coming on
Wednesday."

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.245
It was Monday.
And he comes and he's like,

00:04:40.245 --> 00:04:42.515
"Hey, Iman, heard you're doing
a great job," or whatever.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.616
And I was like --

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.051
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.885
Stared at him until he left.

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.554
And then he came back Wednesday

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.490
and I had written this like
four-page letter.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.393
The first page was like me
gushing over him.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:55.094
The next three pages were
like 70 questions

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.662
about the MCU and his life.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.598
And so I gave it to him.
And Sana was basically

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.400
our mediator throughout
this whole conversation.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.803
She's like, "Iman, you have
something for Kevin.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:06.005
Kevin, what do you want to say
to Iman?"

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.441
[ Laughter ]
And it was like really awkward.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.509
And I gave him this letter,
and the next day he called me

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:12.712
and like answered
the first 40 over Zoom.

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:13.913
So yeah.
-Alright.

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:15.681
-I am more comfortable
with the man now.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.016
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.351
-That is very nice to hear.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:21.754
It must be so --
I could only imagine.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:24.557
You've been working for
two years on this project.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:27.025
And now you can finally talk
about it with people.

00:05:27.025 --> 00:05:28.527
You've known secrets.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:30.763
You've known plot points that
you haven't been able to share.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:33.700
Has it been rewarding to talk to
fans who have responded to it?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.801
-Dude, I can breathe.
It's so nice.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.604
I'm like -- I'm not present
on social media publicly

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:41.506
but I do have like a lot of
private accounts.

00:05:41.506 --> 00:05:42.842
Especially on Reddit.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.677
I'm just like arguing with
people about theories.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:46.612
I'm like, "You don't even know
what's coming, man.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:50.082
Like, you're so wrong."
It's so liberating.

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.316
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.316 --> 00:05:54.286
-So you also had to keep
a secret about auditioning

00:05:54.286 --> 00:05:56.088
for this in the first place
from your friends.

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.725
Everyone -- You were planning on
going to college, right?

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:00.426
And just put a pause on that.
-Yeah.

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.727
I was like with my friends.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.496
I was planning rooming together
at university.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.866
Little did they know that was
not going to happen

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.401
'cause I got the part in front
of them

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.269
and they were like, "What?"

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.871
-What could you mean
in front of them?

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.707
-So it was the last day of
high school and we were out

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:17.777
doing stuff and I get this text
from Sarah Finn

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.077
and she's like, "Hey, can you
get on this call?"

00:06:19.077 --> 00:06:20.480
And I was like, "No."

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.148
And then they were like,
"We sent you the link.

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.549
Get on right now."
And I was like, "Okay."

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.551
And I'm in my friend's driveway
and they're watching me

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.953
from the car and I'm trying to
not have a reaction

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:29.722
'cause Kevin Feige's
on my phone.

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.624
It was just --
My brain was spinning.

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.125
And then I get back in the car
and they were like,

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.027
"So what happened? Did you like
win the lottery or something?"

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.395
And I was like, "Basically."

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:38.197
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:39.832
-And then how did you celebrate?

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.066
-Burritos. We got burritos.

00:06:41.066 --> 00:06:42.268
-Yeah. Burritos?
-Yeah.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.370
-Well, I think that
there's no achievement

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.272
that that's not
the proper celebration for.

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.606
-I'd say so.

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:50.075
-What a delight to spend time
with you this evening.

00:06:50.075 --> 00:06:51.376
Congratulations on everything.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:51.376 --> 00:06:53.245
-I just met you
but I don't think

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:54.447
it could have happened to
a nicer person.

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.081
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:56.081 --> 00:06:58.283
You guys, that's Iman Vellani.

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:01.487
All episodes of "Ms. Marvel" are
available now on Disney+.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:02.688
We'll be right back.

